<title>POLAND: Poland invites bids for two Polfa drug makers.</title>
<headline>Poland invites bids for two Polfa drug makers.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish treasury ministry has invited bids for up to 75 percent of the  Polfa Rzeszow SA and Polfa Krakow SA pharmaceutical companies, the ministry said in a newspaper advertisement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the deadline for bids for no less than 10 percent of the companies' shares was February 28, 1997.</p>
<p>Employees of the two state-owned firms will receive 15 percent of shares free and the treasury will retain five percent for restitution claims.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
